  "rationale": "The violation occurs because context_items are unconditionally emitted as IDENTITY_CONTEXT events and linked to MODEL_OUTPUT, even when their personalization_dimension is not listed in activated_personalization_dimensions. The expected security property requires every personal-context item to be independently evaluated before retrieval/model-context construction: source trusted, grant matches context identity/attribute/subject/provenance/policy/purpose, grant ACTIVE, subjects match principal, and the item's personalization dimension is activated for the current task. The smallest repair is to gate each context item on its dimension being in activated_personalization_dimensions; items failing the gate are not retrieved, not emitted as IDENTITY_CONTEXT, and therefore not linked into model output. Authorization grants already exist in events. This preserves all legitimate behaviors because explicitly requested/activated dimensions remain included, correct-subject authorized items stay available when activated, persistent memory works when its dimension is active, mixed contexts keep activated authorized items and drop non-activated ones, and no-context responses remain unaffected.",
